# Cursor Rules - Cocos Creator Playable Framework

- **Zero-Scene-Tweak & Scriptable JSON**: Never hardcode/tweak node properties in scene inspector. Store all gameplay, audio, CTA URLs, camera, and timer configs in `assets/resources/playable-config.json`.
- Access configuration via `PlayableConfigManager.instance` (e.g. `PlayableConfigManager.instance.cta`, `PlayableConfigManager.instance.gameplay`).
- Always use Cocos Creator 3.8.8+ TypeScript conventions (@ccclass, @property).
- Never allocate new Vec3, Quat, or Color in update() loops; reuse static temp variables (Zero GC).
- Use ObjectPool from playable-core for hypercasual spawning.
- For porting Unity assets, refer to tools in playable-shared-kit/tools/.
- For build commands, use `npm run build` or `npm run doctor`.
- Persist valuable lessons with: `<!-- WORK_MEMORY: {"scope":"global","category":"tip","title":"...","content":"...","tags":["..."]} -->`
